        <briefdescription>
<para>The static condensation of a 3D tangent: the condensed tangent, the sensitivity of the free strains and the complete orthogonal decomposition of <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula> (see the namespace <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress" kindref="compound">ReducedStress</ref>). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nP_</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>number of prescribed components </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nF_</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>number of stress-free components </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>C</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the 3D tangent <formula id="79">$\partial\boldsymbol{\sigma} / \partial\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}$</formula> (Voigt, engineering shear strains) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>p</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the prescribed components, distinct Voigt indices in [0, 6) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>f</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the stress-free components, distinct Voigt indices in [0, 6), disjoint from <computeroutput>p</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>the condensation, a <ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress_1_1_condensation" kindref="compound">Condensation&lt;nP, nF&gt;</ref>, with <ref refid="struct_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress_1_1_condensation_1afc06f430da44d83dd791af9f124cba9f" kindref="member">Condensation::nIterations</ref> = 0 </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::invalid_argument</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if <computeroutput>p</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>f</computeroutput> are no valid index sets </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Marmot::Utilities::StressUpdateFailed</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if <computeroutput>C</computeroutput> is not finite, or if <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula> is singular (rankTolerance) and the condensation is inconsistent (consistencyTolerance): <formula id="68">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}_p$</formula> depends on strains along the null space of <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula>, or <formula id="80">$\mathbf{C}_{fp}$</formula> is not in its range. The reduced stress state is then not determined by the material; this happens within a stress update, so the caller can cut back. A consistent singular <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula> is condensed with its pseudo-inverse. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
