          <declname>p</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::array&lt; int, nF_ &gt; &amp;</type>
          <declname>f</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>A reduced stress state of a 3D stress update: Newton&apos;s method on the strains at the stress-free components (see the namespace <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress" kindref="compound">ReducedStress</ref>). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each iteration evaluates <computeroutput>computeStress3D</computeroutput> at the current strain increment and corrects the free strains by  <formula id="81">$\Delta\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f \leftarrow \Delta\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f -
\mathbf{C}_{ff}^{+} \boldsymbol{\sigma}_f$</formula> (minimum norm, see <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress_1a2b38179c3d7b789c69c97eb29451c2dc" kindref="member">condense()</ref>), until  <formula id="82">$\max_i |\sigma_{f_i}|
\leq 10^{-12}\, s$</formula> (convergenceTolerance), or <formula id="83">$10^{-9}\, s$</formula> (relaxedConvergenceTolerance) from the 9th evaluation on. The stress scale <formula id="84">$s$</formula> is the largest stress component <formula id="85">$|\sigma_i|$</formula> (all six) of all evaluations of this call, so the tolerance is relative and unit free, and it is met by a stress state of round-off size; if all stresses vanish, the residual does too. After 15 evaluations without convergence, it throws.</para>
<para>The last evaluation of <computeroutput>computeStress3D</computeroutput> is the one at the converged strain, so additional outputs of the callable (state variables, energies, other derivatives) refer to the converged 3D state.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nP_</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>number of prescribed components </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>nF_</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>number of stress-free components </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>StressUpdate3D</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>callable <computeroutput>void( const Marmot::Math::Vector6d&amp; dStrain, Marmot::Math::Vector6d&amp; stress, Marmot::Math::Matrix6d&amp; dStress_dStrain )</computeroutput>: the 3D stress update for the strain increment <computeroutput>dStrain</computeroutput> from the start of the increment, i.e., every call must reset what the previous call updated (state variables, the stress at the start of the increment, energies). <computeroutput>stress</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>dStress_dStrain</computeroutput> are zeroed before each call. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>computeStress3D</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>the 3D stress update </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">dStrain</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>in: the prescribed strain increments at <computeroutput>p</computeroutput>, an initial guess at <computeroutput>f</computeroutput>, and the given increments (usually zero) at the other components; out: the converged increment </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>p</parametername>
