    <briefdescription>
<para>Reduced stress states by static condensation: some stress components vanish, the strains at them follow. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>In Marmot&apos;s Voigt order <formula id="53">$[11, 22, 33, 12, 13, 23]$</formula> (engineering shear strains), a reduced stress state is defined by the prescribed strain components <formula id="54">$p$</formula> and the stress-free components <formula id="55">$f$</formula>: the strains <formula id="56">$\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p$</formula> are given, <formula id="57">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}_f = \mathbf{0}$</formula> determines the strains <formula id="58">$\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f$</formula>, and the strains at the components in neither set keep their given values (usually zero). With the 3D tangent partitioned into the blocks  <formula id="59">$\mathbf{C}_{pp}, \mathbf{C}_{pf},
\mathbf{C}_{fp}, \mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula>, linearizing <formula id="57">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}_f = \mathbf{0}$</formula> gives the sensitivity of the free strains and the condensed tangent:      <formula id="60">\[  \frac{\partial \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f}{\partial \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p}
    = -\mathbf{C}_{ff}^{-1}\, \mathbf{C}_{fp}, \qquad
  \frac{\partial \boldsymbol{\sigma}_p}{\partial \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p}
    = \mathbf{C}_{pp} - \mathbf{C}_{pf}\, \mathbf{C}_{ff}^{-1}\, \mathbf{C}_{fp}.
\]</formula> Any other derivative is condensed the same way: e.g. a quantity  <formula id="61">$\mathbf{y}(\boldsymbol{\varepsilon},
\mathbf{K})$</formula> with an additional argument <formula id="62">$\mathbf{K}$</formula> has  <formula id="63">$\mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f /
\mathrm{d}\mathbf{K} = -\mathbf{C}_{ff}^{-1}\, \partial\boldsymbol{\sigma}_f / \partial \mathbf{K}$</formula> and   <formula id="64">$\mathrm{d}\mathbf{y} / \mathrm{d}\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p = \partial\mathbf{y} /
\partial\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p + \partial\mathbf{y} / \partial\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f\, \partial
\boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_f / \partial \boldsymbol{\varepsilon}_p$</formula>.</para>
<para>A singular <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula> is admitted if the reduced problem stays consistent, e.g. a fully softened smeared crack without out-of-plane shear stiffness: then <formula id="66">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}^{-1}$</formula> above is the pseudo-inverse <formula id="67">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}^{+}$</formula>, so the strains along the null space of <formula id="65">$\mathbf{C}_{ff}$</formula> are not changed (minimum norm corrections), which is exact as long as neither <formula id="68">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}_p$</formula> nor <formula id="69">$\boldsymbol{\sigma}_f$</formula> depend on them. Otherwise, the reduced stress state is not determined, and StressUpdateFailed is thrown.</para>
<para><ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress_1a6c9eccb1c84b4124824da2c4d4359081" kindref="member">computeReducedStress()</ref> is the iteration of a 3D stress update to such a state, <ref refid="namespace_marmot_1_1_continuum_mechanics_1_1_reduced_stress_1a2b38179c3d7b789c69c97eb29451c2dc" kindref="member">condense()</ref> the algebra of a given tangent. The standard states are defined below: plane stress (planeStressPrescribed, planeStressFree) and uniaxial stress (uniaxialStressPrescribed, uniaxialStressFree). </para>
    </detaileddescription>
